<title>USA: National Steel Corp Q3 net up.</title>
<headline>National Steel Corp Q3 net up.</headline>
<dateline>MISHAWAKA, Ind. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In millions, except per share data)</p>
<p>					     Three Months  Nine Months</p>
<p>				     Ended Sept. 30,  Ended Sept. 30,</p>
<p>					 1996    1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net Sales			 $735.9  $724.8 $2,187.5 $2,214.1</p>
<p> Income from Operations	  27.0    19.4     29.1    121.6</p>
<p> Financing costs (net)	    9.5     8.9     27.6     30.4</p>
<p> Gain on sale of asset	  (3.7)     0.0    (3.7)	0.0</p>
<p>   Total				5.8     8.9     23.9     30.4</p>
<p>Income Before Extraordinary Item</p>
<p>					 24.3    15.6     19.1     90.6</p>
<p>Extraordinary item, net of</p>
<p>   applicable income tax	  0.0     5.4	0.0	5.4</p>
<p> Net Income			  24.3    21.0     15.1     98.0</p>
<p>Net Income Applicable to</p>
<p>   Common Stock		    21.6    18.3     10.9     87.8</p>
<p>PER SHARE DATA APPLICABLE TO COMMON STOCK:</p>
<p>Income Before Extraordinary Item</p>
<p>					 0.50    0.30     0.25     1.94</p>
<p> Extraordinary item		0.00    0.12     0.00     0.12</p>
<p>Net Income Applicable to</p>
<p>   Common Stock		    0.50    0.42     0.25     2.06</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 1996 results included a gain of $3.7 million from the sale of property, as well as adjustments to employee benefit related liabilities, along with the settlement of a dispute with the Pension Benefit Guaranty Corporation regarding a joint venture's benefit plan. These nonrecurring gains totaled approximately $13 million, net of tax. Excluding these items, third quarter net income totaled $11.2 million, or $0.20 per share.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
